hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19614","Hushaym narrated to us, al-Shaybani informed us from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey in the month of Ramadan, and when the sun set he said: Dismount, O so-and-so, and mix gruel for us. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is still day upon you. He said: Dismount and mix. He said: So he did, and handed it to him, and he drank, and when he drank he gestured with his hand toward the west and said: When the sun sets here and the night comes from here, then the fasting person has broken his fast."
"19615","Hushaym narrated to us, al-Shaybani informed us from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid, freedman of Banu Hashim, he said: Ibn Shaddad and Abu Burdah sent me and said: Go to Ibn Abi Awfa and say to him: Abdullah ibn Shaddad and Abu Burdah send greetings to you and say: Did you make advance payments in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for wheat and barley and raisins. He said: Yes, we used to obtain spoils in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we would pay in advance for them in wheat and barley and dates and raisins. I said: With one who had crops or with one who had no crops. He said: We did not ask them about that. He said: And they said to me: Go to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza and ask him. He said: So I went and asked him, and he said the same as Ibn Abi Awfa said."
"19616","He said: And likewise Abu Muawiyah narrated it to us from Zaidah from al-Shaybani, he said: And oil."
"19617","Amr ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman al-Shaybani from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the green jar. He said: I said: Then the white. He said: I do not know."
"19618","Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Yafur, an Abdi and their freedman, narrated to us, he said: I went to Ibn Abi Awfa asking him about locusts. He said: I went on six expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), eating locusts."
"19619","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he said to a man: Dismount and mix gruel for us. And Sufyan once said: O Messenger of Allah. He said: Mix. He said: O Messenger of Allah. He said: Mix. So he mixed and he drank, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank he gestured with his hand toward the night: When you see the night approaching from here, then the fasting person has broken his fast."
"19620","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Shaybani from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: We came upon donkeys outside the village, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Overturn the pots with what is in them. I mentioned that to Said ibn Jubayr, and he said: He only forbade them because they used to eat filth."
"19621","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Ubayd ibn al-Hasan from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, would say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter."
"19622","Ismail narrated to us, Layth informed us from Mudrik from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate and say: O Allah, purify me with snow and hail and cold water. O Allah, purify my heart from sins as You purified the white garment from filth, and distance between me and my sins as You distanced between the east and the west. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not humble itself, and from a soul that is not satisfied, and from a supplication that is not heard, and from knowledge that does not benefit. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from these four. O Allah, I ask You for a God-fearing life, and a sound death, and a return that is not disgraceful."
"19623","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from al-Qasim al-Shaybani from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: Muadh came to Yemen, or he said: Syria, and saw the Christians prostrating to their patriarchs and bishops, so he conceived in himself that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more deserving to be honored. When he came he said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw the Christians prostrating to their patriarchs and bishops, so I conceived in myself that you are more deserving to be honored. He said: If I were commanding anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the wife to prostrate to her husband. And the wife does not fulfill all the right of Allah Mighty and Majestic upon her until she fulfills all the right of her husband upon her, even if he asks her for herself while she is on the back of a camel-saddle, she would give it to him."
"19624","Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me from al-Qasim ibn Awf, a man of Kufah, one of Banu Murrah ibn Hammam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from his father from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: He came to Syria and saw the Christians, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: I said: For what do you do this. They said: This was the greeting of the prophets before us. I said: We are more deserving to do this with our Prophet. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They lied about their prophets as they altered their book. Allah Mighty and Majestic has replaced for us better than that: Peace, the greeting of the people of Paradise."
"19625","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when people brought him their charity, would pray over them. Then my father brought him his charity, and he said: O Allah, send blessings upon the family of Abu Awfa."
"19626","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give glad tidings to Khadijah. He said: Yes, he gave her glad tidings of a house of reed in which there is no noise nor hardship."
"19627","Yahya narrated to us from Ismail, Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah, then circumambulated the House, then went out and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and we used to shield him from the people of Makkah lest anyone shoot him or hit him with anything. I heard him supplicating against the confederates, saying: O Allah, Sender of the Book, Swift in reckoning, Defeater of the confederates, O Allah, defeat them and shake them."
"19628","Waki narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us from Talhah ibn Musarrif, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bequeath anything. He said: No. I said: Then how was the Muslims commanded with bequest. He said: He bequeathed the Book of Allah Mighty and Majestic. Malik ibn Mighwal said: Talhah said, and al-Huzayl ibn Shurahbil said: Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, used to take charge over the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, wished he had found a covenant with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his nose would be bridled with a bridle."
"19629","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us from Ibrahim Abu Ismail al-Saksaki from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not read the Quran, so command me with what suffices me from it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Say: Praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah. He said: The man said it and clenched his fist and counted five with his thumb. He said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for Allah Almighty, so what is for myself. He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me and have mercy on me and grant me health and guide me and provide for me. He said: He said it and clenched his other fist and counted five with his thumb. The man went off having clenched both his fists together, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has filled his two fists with good."
"19630","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And it was in my fathers book: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Faid ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then a boy came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, here is an orphan boy who has a widowed mother and an orphaned sister, feed us from what Allah Almighty has fed you, Allah will give you from what is with Him until you are pleased. Then he mentioned the hadith at length."
"19631","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And it was in my fathers book: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Faid ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, here is a boy on the point of death, it is said to him: Say: There is no god but Allah, and he cannot say it. He said: Did he not say it in his life. He said: Yes. He said: Then what prevented him from it at his death. Then he mentioned the hadith at length. My father did not narrate to us these two hadiths, he struck them out from his book because he was not pleased with the hadith of Faid ibn Abd al-Rahman, and with him he was abandoned in hadith."
"19632","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Mukhtar of Banu Asad, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: Thirst afflicted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions. He said: He alighted at a stopping place, and a vessel was brought, and he began to give his companions to drink, and they began to say: Drink. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who gives drink to the people is the last of them, until he gave them all to drink."
"19633","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman al-Shaybani, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and fasting, and he called the keeper of his drink for drink. The keeper of his drink said to him: If only you would wait until evening, O Messenger of Allah. Then he called him and said to him: If only you would wait until evening, three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the night comes from here, then breaking the fast has become lawful, or a word to this meaning."
"19634","Bahz and Affan, the meaning, said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us— Affan said in his hadith: Said ibn Jumhan narrated to us, and Bahz said in his hadith: Said ibn Jumhan narrated to me— he said: We were with Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa fighting the Khawarij, and a boy of Ibn Abi Awfa had joined the Khawarij, so we called him: O Fayruz, this is Ibn Abi Awfa. He said: What an excellent man, if only he emigrated. He said: What does the enemy of Allah say. He said: He says: What an excellent man, if only he emigrated. He said: An emigration after my emigration with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), repeating it three times. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Glad tidings to whoever kills them and then they kill him. Affan said in his hadith: And they kill him, three times."
"19635","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Hashraj ibn Nubatah al-Absi, a Kufan, narrated to us, Said ibn Jumhan narrated to me, he said: I met Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa while he was blind, and I greeted him. He said to me: Who are you. I said: I am Said ibn Jumhan. He said: Then what happened to your father. He said: I said: The Azariqah killed him. He said: May Allah curse the Azariqah, may Allah curse the Azariqah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that they are the dogs of the Fire. He said: I said: The Azariqah alone or all the Khawarij. He said: Rather all the Khawarij. He said: I said: The ruler wrongs people and does to them. He said: He took my hand and pressed it with his hand a severe press, then said: Woe to you, O Ibn Jumhan, keep to the great mass, keep to the great mass. If the ruler listens to you, then come to him in his house and inform him of what you know, and if he accepts from you, and otherwise then leave him, for you are not more knowledgeable than him."
"19636","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said— and he was of the companions of the tree— he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a man brought him his charity, would say: O Allah, send blessings upon the family of so-and-so. He said: Then my father brought him his charity, and he said: O Allah, send blessings upon the family of Abu Awfa."
"19637","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Hajari informed us, he said: I went out in the funeral of the daughter of Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, while he was upon a black mule of his, meaning black. He said: The women began to say to his guide: Put him ahead of the funeral, and he did. He said: I heard him saying to him: Where is the funeral. He said: He said: Behind you. He said: He did that once or twice, then said: Did I not forbid you to put me ahead of the funeral. He said: He heard a woman beating her chest, and once he said: lamenting. He said: Be quiet, did I not forbid you from this. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid lamentations. Let one of you shed of her tears whatever she wishes. When the funeral was placed, he stepped forward and said four takbirs over it, then stood a while, and some of the people prompted him with glorification, so he turned away and said: Did you think I would say a fifth takbir. They said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said the fourth takbir, would stand a while. When the funeral was placed, he sat and we sat with him, and he was asked about the meat of domestic donkeys. He said: On the day of Khaybar, domestic donkeys met us outside the village, and the people fell upon them and slaughtered them, and the pots were boiling with some of them when a caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: Pour them out, so we poured them out. And I saw upon Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa a green cloak of silk-mixed wool."
